{
  "id": "Compound::DB06637 - Gene::3742",
  "verbalization": "Dalfampridine is likely to interact with Kcna6 through a shared pathway involving delayed rectifier potassium channels. The evidence suggests that Dalfampridine binds to Kcnf1 or Kcnv2, which are both involved in delayed rectifier potassium channel activity. This activity is then participated in by Kcna6, indicating a functional link between these channels. The high scores from the three paths suggest a consistent relationship, with Dalfampridine potentially modulating the activity of delayed rectifier potassium channels, which in turn influence Kcna6. The overlapping roles of Kcnf1 and Kcnv2 in this pathway imply that Dalfampridine may act through a common mechanism, possibly by enhancing or inhibiting the function of these channels. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that Dalfampridine exerts its effects on Kcna6 via a pathway involving delayed rectifier potassium channels.",
